        "id": 52976,
        "name": "Koey",
        "username": "Koey",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koey/{size}/2187_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-14T00:03:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't understand the distinction between \"Ascension style\" and \"Dominion style\".&nbsp; Elaboration?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I have played dominion, but not ascension.</p>\n<p>You can try the web client to get a better idea of Deck Building genre. The board game style is definitely better but this implementation is quite decent.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://play.goko.com/Dominion/gameClient.html\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://play.goko.com/Dominion/gameClient.html</a></p>",
